---
const images = [
  { src: "/images/category-safaris.avif", alt: "Safari vehicle crossing the savanna" },
  { src: "/images/lodge-siringit-camp.jpg", alt: "Comfortable lodge tent interior" },
  { src: "/images/why-travel-cheetah.jpg", alt: "Cheetah resting in golden grass" },
  { src: "/images/itinerary-tarangire-ngorongoro.jpg", alt: "Elephants beneath the baobabs in Tarangire" },
  { src: "/images/lodge-zuri-zanzibar.webp", alt: "Relaxed seating inside a safari vehicle" },
  { src: "/images/destination-tanzania.avif", alt: "Zebras grazing on the Serengeti plains" },
];
---

<section class="w-full max-w-5xl mx-auto mt-20 md:mt-32 flex flex-col items-center px-4 sm:px-8">
  <h2 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl text-center leading-tight text-primary">
    How a Private Safari With Atlas Works
  </h2>
  <div class="w-16 h-[3px] bg-primary mt-4 mb-8"></div>

  <div class="flex flex-col gap-5 max-w-[820px]">
    <p class="font-body text-base text-center leading-[162.5%] text-text">
      We only organize safaris in Tanzania — the Serengeti, Ngorongoro Crater, Tarangire and
      the parks around them. It is your vehicle and your guide for the whole trip, so when you
      want to stay another hour with a leopard, you stay. Lions, elephants and giraffe are often
      a few metres from the window.
    </p>
    <p class="font-body text-base text-center leading-[162.5%] text-text">
      By evening your guide brings you to a lodge or tented camp we picked for your budget and
      your pace, where you can eat well and sleep in the quiet. The next morning you leave early
      — the animals hunt in the cool hours, and the plains are yours before anyone else is up.
    </p>
    <p class="font-body text-base text-center leading-[162.5%] text-text">
      A Tanzania trip is not only game drives. Add a hot-air balloon over the Serengeti, a
      morning with a Maasai or Hadzabe community, a walking safari, coffee at Materuni Falls,
      Kilimanjaro, or a week on Zanzibar. Because the trip is private, any of it can be moved,
      added or dropped — even once you are here.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 w-full mt-10">
    {
      images.map((image) => (
        <div class="h-48 sm:h-56 md:h-64 rounded-lg overflow-clip">
          <img src={image.src} alt={image.alt} class="size-full object-cover" />
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</section>
